{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/publications/uk-india-trade-deal-double-contributions-convention-explainer","content_id":"7a213330-f288-4136-b8a5-fe2c2ae52174","description":"Information on the Double Contributions Convention that the UK and India have agreed.","details":{"attachments":[{"attachment_type":"html","command_paper_number":"","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"9348690","isbn":"","title":"UK-India Double Contributions Convention (DCC) explainer ","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"/government/publications/uk-india-trade-deal-double-contributions-convention-explainer/uk-india-double-contributions-convention-dcc-explainer"}],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>A Double Contributions Convention (<abbr title=\"Double Contributions Convention\">DCC</abbr>) is an agreement that ensures employees moving between the UK and India only pay social security contributions in one country at a time. This document explains what the UK and India have committed to in relation to a <abbr title=\"Double Contributions Convention\">DCC</abbr>, as set out in the side letter to the Trade Agreement.</p>\n\n<p>This explainer covers:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>what a Double Contribution Convention is</li>\n  <li>how it works</li>\n  <li>what has been agreed to on the UK-India Double Contributions Convention</li>\n  <li>the potential impacts of a UK-India Double Contributions Convention <br>\n<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"Reciprocal agreement where UK and Indian detached workers will pay solely into their home social security scheme when they are temporarily working abroad for an agreed maximum period has been extended from 36 to 60 months.","public_timestamp":"2026-06-17T14:21:51Z"},{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2025-07-23T21:30:00Z"}],"document_type_label":"Promotional material","emphasised_organisations":["aa750cdf-7925-429d-a2b3-0d9fa47d2c48","1994e0e4-bd19-4966-bbd7-f293d6e